     Prepare medium
     5            We generally prepare two or three 10L carboys at a time
                  To 1 L of H2O, add 33.33g of Red Sea Salt
                  Dissolve by shaking (20 min on agitator)
                  Heat seawater during 20min at 100°C
                   Red Sea Salt Red Sea

     6            Add to seawater under laminar flow hood the following nutriments that have been
                  autoclaved (except for vitamin)
                  In Roscoff, we generally also add 1 mL NaNO3 1M for Synechococcus (useless for
                  Prochlorococcus but it does not affect the growth)

              1     Quantit    Compound                                                Final
                    y                                                                  concentration
              2 1.0 mL         Hepes-NaOH 1M (ph 7,5) - See receipe above              1mM
              3 1.0 mL         Na2-EDTA/FeCl3 - See receipe above                      2µMa
              4 1.0 mL         Sodium Phosphate (NaPO4) 50mM (pH 7,5) - See            50µM
                               receipe above




protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n   June 12, 2019                        5/6
              5 1.0 mL         Ammonium Sulfate 400mM (NH4)2-SO4                   400µM
              6 0.1 mLb        Trace metals “Gaffron+Se” - See receipe above
              7                Cyanocobalamin 10mg/L (Vit. B12)                    1µg/Lc
                   0.1 mL

               Note

               a - The original recipe is 8 µM (Rippka et al 2000 IJSEM 50, 1833–1847). But it works
               fine for Prochlorococcus...
               b - If one adds 0.1 mL par L, the final concentration of Gaffron in the PCR-S11
               medium is actually twice more than in the original PCR-S11 recipe.
               c - 10 times less than in the original receipe. Again this seems sufficient...

     7      Filter the medium on 0.2 micron filter




